d["threads_out"]=[
{"to":"v3:endeavour","note":"Banks and Solander had met Tahitians on the Endeavour in 1769; that voyage is why the Admiralty sent Mai to them in 1774."},
{"to":"v4:transits-of-venus","note":"Cook's 1769 transit observations at Tahiti began the British connection with the Society Islands that brought Mai to London."},
{"to":"v9:boston-1721","note":"Mai's inoculation by Thomas Dimsdale in 1774 used variolation, the method introduced in Boston in 1721; Dimsdale had inoculated Catherine the Great in 1768."},
{"to":"v9:balmis-1803","note":"Within a generation Jenner's vaccine replaced the variolation used on Mai, and the Balmis expedition carried it around the Spanish empire."}
]

